Moved by Cr Smith, seconded by Cr MacRae

That:- 

(i) the Hon Minister for Planning and Infrastructure be requested, in response to her letter dated 4 December 2002, that in view of the Council's legal advice dated 25 March 2003 and 8 April 2003 and the Council's clear understanding that the net proceeds from the sale of Areas "F" and "G" would be utilised in determining the value of the agreement towards achieving $11.5 million and resulting in a shared return to the Town and the Botanic Gardens and Parks Authority for any proceeds exceeding $11.5 million, to change her position to that detailed in the Council's decision dated 16 December 1996;

Moved by Cr Berry, seconded by Cr Bradley

That:

(i) the report detailing the options for consideration for addressing speed and volume of traffic in Pandora Drive be received;

(ii) the development of the intersection of Empire Avenue / Durston Road be reviewed, in conjunction with the City of Stirling and the adjacent residents, and a proposal be submitted for Council consideration;

(iii) origin/destination surveys be completed on Pandora Drive traffic for consideration when evaluating further traffic management options;

(iv) the Administration be requested to evaluate traffic treatment options for Pandora Drive for presentation to Council and subsequent canvassing with residents.
